Notebook[{
Cell["HypergraphEventPlot", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"fec76953-06e5-4040-8bd6-9033a8bd603c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"HypergraphEventPlot", "[", "event", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"c0d26704-a181-6c40-8ab6-81a2a0b75adc"],
 " ",
 "draws a rewriting event: what it acted on with the match highlighted, an \
arrow, and what it made with the created vertices and edges highlighted."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"a7528f66-7086-5b43-9d4d-39329d5caf3c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"HypergraphEventPlot", "[", 
    RowBox[{"rule", ",", " ", "hg"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"55674c2e-db57-134a-bae1-7cb477ff1987"],
 " ",
 "gives one picture for every way rule matches hg."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"79b51f84-650e-5a4f-8aa5-1eb6bc83b4b1"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"c1fef5d4-44a5-ce4f-b7b9-0a99cedfc806"],

Cell["\<\
An event is an association of the kind HypergraphRuleApply gives. Its \"Input\
\" key is the hypergraph the event acted on, which is what makes the left \
half drawable.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"885ed290-1c16-8d4b-a05c-067a8ed4f434"],

Cell["\<\
Both halves are drawn on the same layout, so that a vertex which did not move \
does not appear to. A vertex the event created has no place in that layout \
and is settled among its neighbours, which puts a vertex inserted into an \
edge between that edge's ends.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"717e4050-847b-6743-9154-d3e45e49ab01"],

Cell["\<\
The created edges are found from \"EdgeOrigins\" rather than by looking for \
edges equal to \"NewEdges\": in a multiset two edges of equal value are still \
two edges, and searching by value would highlight one that was merely carried \
over.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"42f7d9c3-47ec-c94f-932d-c96a49aa0ef2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The highlight styles, \"PanelSize\" and \"SharedCoordinates\" are as in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphRulePlot", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"f7f8c908-acd6-c24e-b153-0a95946ef3f6"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"5d10735e-a839-484e-95a1-5625abf420da"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is the picture a rewriting system draws for an event vertex of its ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphCausalGraph", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"5699d088-1976-b747-8913-acbbfe8350fa"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"7575a2c2-5ef5-784c-82b9-ca1e396bd4df"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"2a2f7556-7b91-074a-a0b6-89e70d82a0a6"],

Cell["\<\
Subdividing one edge of a path. The matched edge is red on the left, the two \
edges that replaced it are red on the right:\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"665dad4a-1624-274f-a20e-daeeed1ad200"],

Cell["\<\
event = First @ HypergraphRule[{{1, 2}}, {{1, 3}, {3, 2}}][Hypergraph[{{1, \
2}, {2, 3}}]];
HypergraphEventPlot[event, \"PanelSize\" -> 130]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"be2291be-1507-914e-8b9b-f5096cb91f35"],

